Commentary of al-Nasafi (Madarik al-Tanzil) on surah 64, verse 14:

﴿O you who have believed, indeed, among your spouses and your children are enemies to you﴾. I.e., among spouses there are those who are hostile to their husbands and quarrel with them, and among children there are those who are hostile to their fathers and disobey them.

﴿So beware of them﴾. The pronoun refers to the enemy, i.e., to the spouses and the children all together. That is: since you know that these do not exist without an enemy, be on guard against them and do not feel secure from their harms and their evil.

﴿And if you pardon﴾ them, when you become aware of hostility from them and do not respond to them with the like of it;

﴿and overlook﴾, i.e., turn away from rebuke;

﴿and forgive﴾, i.e., conceal their sins;

﴿then indeed, Allah is Forgiving and Merciful﴾, He will forgive your sins and remove your misdeeds. It is said: some people wanted to make hijrah (migration) away from Makkah, but their spouses and children discouraged them and said, "You will leave and abandon us." So they felt compassion for them and stayed. Then, when they later migrated and saw that those who had preceded them had gained understanding in the religion (p-٤٩٤), they wished to punish their spouses and children, and so pardon was made appealing to them.
